{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the break of dawn, thou shalt arise and make thy way to the airport, where thy journey to Japan doth commence. Take heed, for this adventure of a fortnight's length requires careful planning and a spirit of exploration.\n\nOn the first day, thou shalt arrive in the bustling city of Tokyo. After settling into thine accommodations, ventur'st forth to explore the city. Visit the Senso-ji temple, where incense doth fill the air and the sound of prayer rings in thy ears.\n\nThe following day, discover the wonders of the Ueno Park, where cherry blossoms doth bloom and museums abound. Perchance, thou mayest find thyself lost in the beauty of the National Museum, or the tranquility of the Ueno Zoo.\n \\_\nOn the third day, take a respite from the city's hustle and bustle and journey to Nikko, a city nestled in the mountains. There, thou shalt find the Toshogu shrine, a magnificent structure dedicated to the first shogun of Japan. Marvel at the intricate carvings and the majesty of the surrounding forests.\n\nOn the fourth day, return to Tokyo and visit the Meiji shrine, where the spirit of Emperor Meiji and Empress Shoken doth reside. Pay thy respects and bask in the serenity of the shrine's surroundings.\n\nOn the fifth day, explore the city of Hakone, known for its hot springs and views of Mount Fuji. Take a boat ride on Lake Ashi and soak in the natural beauty of the area.\n\nOn the sixth day, journey to the ancient city of Kyoto. There, thou shalt find the Fushimi Inari shrine, with its iconic red torii gates. Walk the winding paths and lose thyself in the peacefulness of the shrine.\n\nOn the seventh day, visit the Kinkaku-ji temple, also known as the Golden Pavilion, and marvel at its beauty. Reflect on the serenity of the temple and its surroundings.\n\nOn the eighth day, discover the wonders of Nara, a city filled with temples and parks. Visit the Todai-ji temple and gaze upon the Great Buddha, a massive bronze statue of the Buddha Vairocana.\n\nOn the ninth day, take a break from sightseeing and indulge in traditional Japanese activities. Perhaps, try a tea ceremony or learn the art of origami.\n\nOn the tenth day, explore the city of Osaka. Discover the Osaka Castle, a magnificent structure with a rich history. Stroll through the castle's gardens and take in the beauty of the area.\n\nOn the eleventh day, venture to Himeji and visit the Himeji Castle, a magnificent structure known for its white exterior. Learn about its history and marvel at its beauty.\n\nOn the twelfth day, return to Tokyo and prepare for thy journey home. Take this time to reflect on the wonders thou hast seen and the memories thou hast made.\n\nOn the thirteenth day, depart from Japan with a heart full of joy and memories that will last a lifetime. Fare thee well, Japan, and may we meet again.\n\nAnd so, with this itinerary, I have plotted out a journey of discovery and wonder. I hope it bringeth thee joy and fulfillment, and that thou returneth home with memories that will last a lifetime. Safe travels, good adventurer.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.16018113493919373}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.013940464705228806}, {"token": "break", "logprob": -1.4145479202270508}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-06}, {"token": "dawn", "logprob": -0.04357367381453514}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002896366349887103}, {"token": "thou", "logprob": -0.02207924984395504}, {"token": "sh", "logprob": -0.0010748092317953706}, {"token": "alt", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "arise", "logprob": -0.03864968568086624}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.1324817933200393e-05}, {"token": "make", "logprob": -0.08887630701065063}, {"token": "thy", "logprob": -0.09123393893241882}, {"token": "way", "logprob": -1.9550132492440753e-05}, {"token": "to", "logprob": -0.0002051381452474743}, {"token": "the", "